2. Data TypesJavaScript data types are broken down into Primitives (stored by value) and Objects (stored by reference). There are 8 total data types:CategoryData TypeDescriptionExamplePrimitiveNumberDouble-precision 64-bit binary format (integers & floats).let price = 99.99;PrimitiveStringTextual data wrapped in quotes or backticks."Hello World"PrimitiveBooleanLogical entity containing true or false.let isAdmin = true;PrimitiveUndefinedAutomatically assigned to a declared variable without a value.let x;PrimitiveNullIntentional absence of any object value.let record = null;PrimitiveBigIntNumeric values larger than the standard Number limit.9007199254740991nPrimitiveSymbolUnique, immutable identifier.Symbol('id')ReferenceObjectKey-value pairs used to store collections of data.
